Lima (https://github.com/lima-vm/lima)
Copyright The Lima Authors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

  Files that reproduce what Lima's guest boot scripts and guest agent write,
  so that those scripts find them up to date at boot. Some must stay
  byte-identical to Lima's output, so they carry no notice of their own:
    spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/etc/systemd/system/lima-guestagent.service
      (Lima's lima-guestagent.TEMPLATE.service, rendered)
    spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/etc/sysctl.d/99-lima.conf
    spike/alpine/rootfs/etc/sysctl.d/99-lima.conf
      (the lines Lima's 20-rootless-base.sh writes)
    spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/etc/systemd/system/user@.service.d/lima.conf
      (20-rootless-base.sh)
    spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/etc/systemd/resolved.conf.d/00-lima-enable-mdns.conf
      (06-enable-mdns-on-systemd.sh)
    spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10-acceptenv-colorterm.conf
    spike/alpine/rootfs/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/10-acceptenv-colorterm.conf
      (11-colorterm-environment.sh)
  The kernel module list of Lima's 00-modprobe.sh, in
    spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/usr/lib/systemd/system/lima-modules.service
    spike/nixos/lima.nix
    spike/alpine/rootfs/etc/init.d/cpmodules
  lima-init (spike/mkosi/mkosi.extra/usr/libexec/lima-init and its Alpine
  port) reimplements, without cloud-init, the parts of Lima's cloud-init
  user-data these images need, after the approach of Lima's WSL2 driver
  (pkg/driver/wsl2/boot.Linux/02-no-cloud-init-setup.sh), and the
  /etc/environment handling of Lima's 07-etc-environment.sh.

